WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.222 --> 00:00:02.057
- I think the fire crotch thing started

00:00:02.057 --> 00:00:04.291
way before the Lindsay Lohan time.

00:00:04.291 --> 00:00:05.999
Ever since, I guess, I hit puberty.

00:00:05.999 --> 00:00:08.189
(techno music)

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:09.734
Hi, my name is AJ, and I'm a redhead.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:11.362
This week, I'm gonna go blonde.

00:00:11.362 --> 00:00:12.539
My color red, I feel like it's slightly

00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:15.497
different from the average Irish redhead,

00:00:15.497 --> 00:00:17.127
'cause I'm actually not even Irish at all.

00:00:17.127 --> 00:00:18.671
And I'm the only one with red hair.

00:00:18.671 --> 00:00:20.365
Both of my siblings have dark brown hair,

00:00:20.365 --> 00:00:22.318
dark brown eyes, but my mom has red hair.

00:00:22.318 --> 00:00:25.076
I feel like I used to
find, "ginger," offensive,

00:00:25.076 --> 00:00:28.005
but I actually call myself,
King of the Gingers.

00:00:28.005 --> 00:00:31.131
- When I was asked about
dyeing my hair, I said no.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.913
- I personally would never dye my hair.

00:00:32.913 --> 00:00:34.376
- I think redheads are unicorns.

00:00:34.376 --> 00:00:38.029
It seems like such a cool, unique thing,

00:00:38.029 --> 00:00:39.776
that not a lot of people get.

00:00:39.776 --> 00:00:41.077
- I've always been nervous about getting

00:00:41.077 --> 00:00:42.338
back to the original color, I guess.

00:00:42.338 --> 00:00:44.770
Being a redhead is definitely
a huge part of my identity.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.067
- Definitely been told throughout my life

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:47.937
not to ever dye my hair.

00:00:47.937 --> 00:00:50.576
- I don't think redheads should
dye their hair any color.

00:00:50.576 --> 00:00:52.077
- Every time I go to a hair dresser,

00:00:52.077 --> 00:00:54.073
they compliment my red hair.

00:00:54.073 --> 00:00:56.799
They try so hard to get
the same exact color,

00:00:56.799 --> 00:00:59.116
but they always tell me
how unsuccessful they are.

00:00:59.116 --> 00:01:00.703
For my friends who already
know me, it's gonna

00:01:00.703 --> 00:01:03.706
come off as a real shock because
they do love my red hair.

00:01:03.706 --> 00:01:05.776
I get attention as is with red hair,

00:01:05.776 --> 00:01:09.943
but I think going blonde, I'm
gonna get even more attention.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:14.178
- My name is Yuichi, hairstylist today.

00:01:14.178 --> 00:01:15.848
We do the full highlights.

00:01:15.848 --> 00:01:19.416
- My feelings towards my red
hair has definitely changed.

00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:21.369
In the beginning, I didn't
really think much about it.

00:01:21.369 --> 00:01:23.238
As I got into high school, I was

00:01:23.238 --> 00:01:25.147
probably the only one with red hair.

00:01:25.147 --> 00:01:27.622
I definitely was picked
on for being a redhead.

00:01:27.622 --> 00:01:30.342
They would call me
carrot-top, fire crotch,

00:01:30.342 --> 00:01:31.175
all of the above.

00:01:31.175 --> 00:01:34.976
- And then, we do the permanent
color at the same time.

00:01:34.976 --> 00:01:37.369
So we rinse off, check the color.

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:39.520
- I think women with
red hair are glorified

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.402
within society, opposed
to men, who are kind of

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:46.257
looked at or have the stereotype
of being nerdy, geeky.

00:01:46.257 --> 00:01:48.897
There are a million women leading

00:01:48.897 --> 00:01:49.992
actress roles with red hair.

00:01:49.992 --> 00:01:52.143
The men red headed roles are always

00:01:52.143 --> 00:01:53.408
the best friend or the geek.

00:01:53.408 --> 00:01:55.265
Here in L.A., I don't think I really

00:01:55.265 --> 00:01:56.899
know of any other redheads.

00:01:56.899 --> 00:01:58.934
I haven't dated a redhead before,

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:03.306
but I've definitely
fooled around with one.

00:02:03.306 --> 00:02:05.617
Took about two hours
from beginning to end.

00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:08.117
Eager to see what I look like.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.424
Oh my God.

00:02:11.424 --> 00:02:13.779
(AJ laughs)

00:02:13.779 --> 00:02:14.612
Wow.

00:02:14.612 --> 00:02:16.058
I look like a completely different person.

00:02:16.058 --> 00:02:17.273
I think I'm giving off that,

00:02:17.273 --> 00:02:18.814
I don't know, California beach vibe?

00:02:18.814 --> 00:02:20.480
I think I look tanner
a little bit, actually.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.313
Looks great.

00:02:21.313 --> 00:02:23.604
I do like it, it's definitely different.

00:02:23.604 --> 00:02:25.511
It's gonna take a little
bit to get used to.

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:27.342
I think I will be perceived differently

00:02:27.342 --> 00:02:29.532
by people who don't know
me, also by my friends, too.

00:02:29.532 --> 00:02:31.846
So, now that I'm blonde,
I'm going to live the

00:02:31.846 --> 00:02:34.445
rest of the week and see
how everybody reacts to me,

00:02:34.445 --> 00:02:37.003
and see if it's any different
from being a ginger.

00:02:37.003 --> 00:02:40.086
(steady dance music)

00:02:42.691 --> 00:02:44.616
Saw myself, slightly freaked out,

00:02:44.616 --> 00:02:47.165
seeing that I didn't know who that was.

00:02:47.165 --> 00:02:49.029
I did tell a couple of my co-workers.

00:02:49.029 --> 00:02:51.139
They've only known me as a redhead.

00:02:51.139 --> 00:02:53.171
We shall see how people react today.

00:02:53.171 --> 00:02:54.171
- Oh my God!

00:02:56.907 --> 00:02:58.656
- I've had some interesting interactions

00:02:58.656 --> 00:03:00.651
with people who had previously known me.

00:03:00.651 --> 00:03:04.247
There have been a lot of
Game of Thrones references.

00:03:04.247 --> 00:03:05.957
- You look like a Targaryan.

00:03:05.957 --> 00:03:08.153
- And Ken doll references as well

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:10.184
from co-workers and clients.

00:03:10.184 --> 00:03:12.249
There's also been a lot
of, "You look great,

00:03:12.249 --> 00:03:14.606
"except I prefer you as a redhead."

00:03:14.606 --> 00:03:16.112
- I believe gingers should
never dye their hair.

00:03:16.112 --> 00:03:17.496
Go back, AJ!

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:19.849
- Personally, I almost feel
like I'm wearing a mask,

00:03:19.849 --> 00:03:22.941
being blonde because, I've
been red my entire life,

00:03:22.941 --> 00:03:25.512
and it's almost like I'm not
even being true to myself.

00:03:25.512 --> 00:03:27.179
I slightly miss being a redhead.

00:03:27.179 --> 00:03:29.982
I had somebody at the gym
actually comment and say,

00:03:29.982 --> 00:03:32.986
I am one of six redheads
that actually come,

00:03:32.986 --> 00:03:36.323
and now I'm literally just
like everybody else there.

00:03:36.323 --> 00:03:37.773
So something else that I noticed,

00:03:37.773 --> 00:03:40.051
is whenever I run into another redhead,

00:03:40.051 --> 00:03:41.997
I wait for some sort of acknowledgment.

00:03:41.997 --> 00:03:44.967
I was in the grocery store,
probably looked kind of creepy,

00:03:44.967 --> 00:03:47.242
staring at this person, still
waiting for some sort of

00:03:47.242 --> 00:03:49.354
acknowledgement, or even just eye contact.

00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:51.063
I had forgotten that I dyed my hair blond,

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:52.888
and just kind of came
off as a creep, I guess.

00:03:52.888 --> 00:03:54.962
So I'm about to call my dad.

00:03:54.962 --> 00:03:55.795
- [Dad] Hello?

00:03:55.795 --> 00:03:56.628
- Hi, Dad.

00:03:56.628 --> 00:03:57.628
- [Dad] AJ!

00:03:57.628 --> 00:03:59.878
- You don't like me blonde?

00:04:01.644 --> 00:04:03.623
I found myself actually
taking my shirt off

00:04:03.623 --> 00:04:05.574
during my workout class today,

00:04:05.574 --> 00:04:07.358
which I have never done before.

00:04:07.358 --> 00:04:09.958
I walked into work this morning,
and one of my instructors,

00:04:09.958 --> 00:04:11.581
first thing that came out of his mouth,

00:04:11.581 --> 00:04:13.495
"You look so much more approachable!"

00:04:13.495 --> 00:04:15.835
What did I look like when I had red hair?

00:04:15.835 --> 00:04:17.726
So as I talk a little bit more

00:04:17.726 --> 00:04:19.459
to my friends about being blond,

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:22.100
opposed to being a
redhead, I've noticed that,

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.892
although we're thought of as fiery

00:04:23.892 --> 00:04:26.621
or temperamental, we're apparently

00:04:26.621 --> 00:04:28.652
the least shy of the hair colors,

00:04:28.652 --> 00:04:30.477
which I don't know if I
completely agree with that,

00:04:30.477 --> 00:04:33.294
because growing up, I
definitely was a lot more shy,

00:04:33.294 --> 00:04:35.202
until I got comfortable in my own skin.

00:04:35.202 --> 00:04:37.595
Here in Los Angeles, I do
feel that being a redhead,

00:04:37.595 --> 00:04:39.222
I stand out a little bit more.

00:04:39.222 --> 00:04:40.929
Right now, I kinda feel like I blend

00:04:40.929 --> 00:04:42.395
in when I walk down the street.

00:04:42.395 --> 00:04:43.739
I don't know if I feel like

00:04:43.739 --> 00:04:45.285
I would actually go blonde again.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.554
I mean, I like it, I enjoy it,

00:04:46.554 --> 00:04:50.373
but I do feel like this is
hiding my identity a little bit.

00:04:50.373 --> 00:04:53.590
Being a ginger is so far into who I am.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:55.336
I can't see myself going any other way.

00:04:55.336 --> 00:04:57.720
Maybe blonde highlights,
every now and then.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:00.887
(mid-tempo pop music)

